From 6b6b247e2b7885b56611fec347f23df25dcae646 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plsy1 <39407459+plsy1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:58:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: careful mode (BPFTIME_CAREFUL=1) for per-thread comm
 and identity

Dnext for the paper's N5a/N5b. A switch read once at load, off by default;
off, the new agent interposers only forward to libc and the helpers take the
old paths.

N5a: bpf_get_current_comm returns the calling thread's comm with the kernel
helper's semantics (16 bytes, at most 15 characters, NUL padded), cached per
thread and refilled with prctl(PR_GET_NAME). The agent interposes
prctl(PR_SET_NAME) and pthread_setname_np and brackets each rename: no refill
during it, and the comm epoch is bumped at its end.

N5b: the agent interposes vfork/__vfork (frameless asm stub), _Fork,
clone/__clone, posix_spawn(p), pidfd_spawn(p), system and popen/_IO_popen.
They bump the identity epoch before the call; spawns whose child shares the
caller's TLS mark the thread as spawning (no caching meanwhile); a clone with
CLONE_VM and no CLONE_SETTLS that runs concurrently marks the TLS block shared
for good; the children of a raw _Fork and of a clone without CLONE_VM reset
the per-process state the fork handlers would (identity, pid namespace, perf
shard cache, probe_read/write pid, host NSpid cache). A vfork-like child that
changes its credentials turns the credential cache off.

Caches are used in careful mode only if the process binds every interposer
(LD_PRELOAD); under dlmopen or late Frida injection identity and comm are read
on every call. Not covered: raw system calls, writes to /proc/.../comm, the
GLIBC_2.2.5 compat posix_spawn(p) (captured and forwarded to the default
version even with the switch off), and vfork on non-x86 (caches stay off).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
